# The plug release signing key.
#
# ONE key at a time, on purpose. One key makes replacing it and revoking it the
# same act: ship a plug carrying the new key and the old one stops being accepted
# by everybody, with no second step anyone can forget. A list of trusted keys
# would make recovery from a LOST key easier, and would make recovery from a
# STOLEN one worse, because the stolen key stays trusted until somebody
# remembers to delete its line.
#
# Replacing it forces a reinstall of every CLI in the field, immediately: a
# signature that does not verify is refused, full stop. That is the accepted
# cost. Reinstalling is one command and the
# install path carries no signature check, by design: it is a deliberate act
# aimed at a host the user typed, which is exactly what the fetch path is not.
#
# The private half lives in the PLUG_RELEASE_KEY secret and in a vault, and
# nowhere in this repository. See RELEASING.md.
#
# issued 2026-08-31
XGAZ8rNXnw05RcsYJn+OPMvQWfMzu6cs7FzHay1jLD4=
